steel production is one of the most  polluting industries of the world  accounting for about seven percent of  the world's carbon emissions  now three swedish industrial companies  are joining forces for change  i'm here in lulio in northern sweden  close to the arctic circle  and this is where three industrial  giants have formed a partnership to set  up the first fossil free value chain to  produce green steel  and this site here  is  the entrance to hydrogen cave  which will be vital in this venture  so we're standing here in liblio  in this hydrogen storage  a key part of the venture is to develop  a hydrogen storage system so there will  be a steady supply of the fuel for the  production process  hydrogen  is used in the hybrid in the process  replacing coal when we turn iron ore  into iron um  by using hydrogen from fossil free  electricity instead of coal we remove  the source of emissions from this  process  you know just a couple of weeks ago we  were able to produce the first  fossa-free steel in the world and this  is now the next step in building a  completely fossa free value chain  together with our partners lkb and  watenfall a gas tank of about 100 cubic  meters  will be built inside this rock cabin to  store hydrogen if testing is successful  they could make it thousand times bigger  on an industrial scale  this is the product that you get when  you go from iron ore and reduce it  with hydrogen  and  instead of using coke and coal where you  get carbon dioxide you get water as a  boy product and that's when you get  sponge iron this is a raw material  then going to  ssab where you're supposed to to melt  this in an electric arc furnace  and from there  you you get steel that you  roll out  before you have  an end product  ssab has already struck deals with  mercedes-benz  and volvo group  who has recently launched the world's  first fossil-free vehicle  the vehicle behind me is a dumper to be  used in quarries or in mines  it is fully electric it is fully  autonomous and it's built upon fossil  free steel but i think that the beauty  now what we are learning with fossil  free steel is that from a manufacturing  perspective is no difference between the  traditional fossil based steel and  fossil free steel  if you look into a microscope the steel  is identical  transforming energy intensive industries  like steel production will be key to  combat global warming  especially as energy demand is expected  to continue to soar  [Music]  you
 

